  clock: 5  # e821
  nonce: e821  # e821
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, linked-pile L6 investigation): item retitled. Original framing 'Python analyzer lacks explicit stdlib catalog' is FACTUALLY WRONG: python.yaml IS already status=complete with stdlib_provenance + populated stdlib_modules. The actual gap is that the Python analyzer's import-resolution path does NOT consume the catalog (grep stdlib_modules packages/hypergumbo-lang-python/src/ returns empty; only io_boundary.py consumes it for I/O tagging). Decoupled from WI-tukif (catalog-promotion sweep): this is an analyzer-wiring task. Fix scope: io_boundary.py:_load_stdlib_modules → Python analyzer _resolve_import."  # e821
- op: discuss  # 57cd
  at: '2026-06-02T16:12:14Z'  # 57cd
  by: agent  # 57cd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 57cd
  clock: 6  # 57cd
  nonce: 57cd  # 57cd
  message: "Pass-33 face: 2102 substrate `calls` edges target Python ambiguous_names list members (F33.8).\n\nWI-bifih's scope: \"Wire python.yaml stdlib_modules into Python analyzer import resolution.\" The stdlib_modules list (300 entries) exists in `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/io_primitives/python.yaml` but isn't wired through to the analyzer for import resolution. Pass-33 measures a **related** signal in the same YAML — the `ambiguous_names` field:\n\n**Repro.** `python.yaml:ambiguous_names` declares 27 entries:\n```\nread, readline, readlines, write, writelines, close, send, recv, get, post,\nput, delete, head, run, start, stop, encode, decode, open, dump, load, dumps,\nloads, parse, format, save, append\n```\nSubstrate has `calls`-type edges targeting Python nodes with these names:\n```\nTotal edges: 2102\n  get        : 962 edges\n  patch      : 600 edges\n  run        : 149 edges\n  dump       : 76 edges\n  start      : 68 edges\n  ... (more)\n```\n\n**Interpretation.** Python duck-typing makes `obj.get(key)` indistinguishable at the AST layer between `dict.get(...)`, `requests.get(...)`, `queue.get(...)`, `argparse.Namespace.get(...)`, and dozens of other targets. The catalog acknowledges this via the `ambiguous_names` list. The substrate carries 2102 `calls` edges to these names without resolving the receiver — every such edge is structurally low-confidence and consumers (slice, dead-code-maybe, INV-pohik) treat them like high-confidence calls.\n\nThe `ambiguous_names` list IS the producer-side acknowledgment of the same gap WI-bifih documents at the stdlib-modules layer. Two distinct catalog fields, two distinct resolution problems:\n- `stdlib_modules` (300 entries) → known-stdlib import resolution (WI-bifih scope)\n- `ambiguous_names` (27 entries) → method-name receiver-ambiguity (NOT YET WIRED — same shape as WI-bifih)\n\n**Catalog-wired-through gap.** Pass-33 confirms that for both lists, the YAML data is present and well-structured, but neither is consumed at the analyzer level. The `dataflow_patterns` / `io_primitives` / `function_summaries` (catalog top-level keys per F33.6) exist in YAML form but the substrate carries no `meta.io_primitive` / `meta.io_boundary` stamping (cf F33.7 — 0 substrate entries despite the catalog being marked `status: complete` for Python). So the cumulative gap is broader than WI-bifih's title suggests:\n1. `stdlib_modules` not wired to import resolution (WI-bifih scope, already filed)\n2. `ambiguous_names` not wired to receiver-disambiguation (pass-33 finding)\n3. `dataflow_patterns` not wired to edge-stamping (sub-pattern (11) per F30.13 / F33.7)\n\nThe 2102 ambiguous-targeted edges are a known-unknown — the catalog says \"we can't resolve these without context\"; the analyzer ships them as `calls` edges anyway. INV-pohik's high FP rate at dead-code-maybe partly reflects this — `dict.get` calls inflate reachability counts but don't actually reach the named symbol.\n\n**Fix-path candidate** (within or adjacent to WI-bifih scope): when emitting a `calls` edge whose `dst.name` is in the language's `ambiguous_names` list, set `Edge.confidence` to a low value (e.g. 0.4 — the \"variable/computed\" tier per spec §7.464) and/or set a `meta.disambiguation_fallback: true` flag. This makes the receiver-ambiguity visible to downstream consumers (slice can filter; dead-code-maybe can demote).\n\n**No status change.** Pass-33 supplies an `ambiguous_names`-not-wired face that parallels WI-bifih's `stdlib_modules`-not-wired scope. Could be filed as a peer WI or folded into WI-bifih's scope expansion. Probe artifact: `/tmp/p33_outputB.log` section \"B.9\"."  # 57cd
